 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ;; THE PIPELINE MODEL (2026-09-25, roerick) — the unifying status machine
 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 (section pipeline-model
  (doc "THE state pipeline is an ORDERED LIST of state names. It is a first-class
   thing, not a node-kind decision. Any work item (card, note-todo, issue — any
   tree node) carries a pipeline reference + a current position in it. This is
   the unification: one concept (item -> pipeline -> position) rendered by every
   lens, instead of today's two parallel status mechanisms (note/issue `todo`
   slot, 3 states; card `state` field, 5 states).

   RESOLUTION ORDER for an item's effective pipeline (final column set + the
   list the cycle/next machine cycles through):
     a) the pipeline of the LIST the item lives in (the list's `columns`
        field, set via kanban/columns-set / todo/state/columns-for-list) —
        a workstream's list IS its pipeline today;
     b) else the GLOBAL default (todo/state/list).
   OBITUARY (2026-10-05, roerick-approved audit; live on system/main): the
   per-item `pipeline` override (the old tier-a) is RETIRED. Three stacked
   machines made "which states does this card have?" a three-level
   precedence question, forced kanban/stray? other-bucket logic to exist,
   and broke board views for own-pipeline cards. A card that needs a
   different pipeline belongs on a different LIST — the streams ARE lists.
   The stale `pipeline` FIELD on todo-item datums is ignored (not deleted);
   todo/state/pipeline-for-item returns 'list | 'default only. A card can
   ride a different pipeline only by moving to a list that runs it.

   RENDERING CONTRACT (two-level edition): a columnar face (kanban board,
   /pulse) renders, for its chosen pipeline, every item whose state is one of
   that pipeline's columns; anything else lands in the face's trailing
   'other' bucket (kanban/stray? = simply not-a-column since the retirement).
   Nothing is hidden or lost; items simply live on other lists. A pipeline
   with no item ever on it is still a valid pipeline.

   PIPELINES ARE DATA, not code: a pipeline is the `columns` field of a list
   (a JSON array of state-name strings); there is no kernel type and no enum
   to extend. Defining a new pipeline = writing a list. This is why the
   todo/note/issue identity line can converge on one machine: notes/issues
   gain richer status simply by referencing a pipeline; cards already have
   one.

   CONVERGENCE (supersedes work-triage.borg unification-handoff): the card
   `state` machine (5+ states, per-list columns, events, recipes — everything
   the orchestration speaks) is canonical. The notes/issues lens reads the SAME
   machine: an issue or note-todo item is any tree node whose effective
   pipeline + position resolve; the issue/note faces render that status and
   the todo faces render notes/issues nodes whose pipeline matches. A quick
   note-heading todo may keep the outline `todo` 3-state shortcut, but any
   node that wants the full machine references a pipeline.")
  (implements "libs/todo/lib.pp todo/state/columns-for-list + todo/state/next-for-item (two-level)"
              "libs/kanban/lib.pp kanban/stray? (not-a-column)"
              "libs/notes/lib.pp issues lens reads pipeline"
              "libs/workstreams/lib.pp pulse face reads the same columns")
  (status implemented)
  (* agent note (|2026-09-25 roerick: 'we should basically describe the state
     pipeline/status machine as a list. a todo should be able to define its own
     state pipeline. everything in our todo list and our issues log should use
     that same pipeline. but there's no reason we couldn't have todos there with
     other pipelines — if we did that they just wouldn't show up under the
     kanban view.' This section is that model; the 'other bucket' already
     exists (kanban/other-bucket).|) *)
  (* agent note (|2026-09-28 SINGLE-OBJECT ISSUES (shipped; reconciles the
     CONVERGENCE paragraph above). The issue register is now ONE object: a
     kind-tagged todo-item card on the shared Board IS the issue (kind
     BUG/DESIGN/SMELL/CLEANUP/WANT; the card id IS the issue id since
     2026-09-28, board card a21431be). There is no second ledger node and no
     card<->node link to reconcile: notes/issues/add is card-only,
     notes/issues/cards reads kind != "" rows, and /issues renders them live.
     OBITUARY (what/why): the earlier twin-write minted a log/issues ledger
     heading node AND a linked Board card (issue_id field), reconciled by every
     writer; the sync tax was real (a ghost-card resync bug) and board
     visibility needs ONE object per issue. The legacy log/issues note is now a
     FROZEN ARCHIVE at /notes?slug=log/issues — its rows keep
     resolve/reopen/delete so historical issue ids (i-<ts>-<uuid> referenced in
     comments) still resolve, but nothing appends to it. PERF CONTRACT for the
     /issues face: issue-card renders MUST memoize effective pipeline columns
     per LIST (notes/issues/cols-map), never per-row
     columns-for-item/pipeline-for-item — the per-row shape 500'd /issues on the
     route budget.|) *)
  (verify
   (test "an item's effective pipeline = list columns, else the global default (two-level)"
         "a card in a state the board has no column for renders in the other bucket, never hidden"
         "an issue whose node references the work-triage pipeline renders in kanban columns"
         "a new pipeline is just writing a columns list — no kernel type"
         "no todo/card writer reads the per-item `pipeline` field anymore")))


 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ;; PULSE PROJECTION (2026-10-05) — the cross-stream indicator face
 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 (section pulse-projection
  (doc "DECISION (roerick, 2026-10-05): heterogeneous pipelines are the
   reality — a BUG card, an ops stream, and a faces card do not share one
   state machine, and the strict RENDERING CONTRACT above (faces render
   only matching-pipeline items) fragments the view the more streams
   differ. REVISED to two layers.
     - NATIVE (unchanged): each list's columns are its real pipeline;
       boards stay per-list at /kanban?list=<id>. The shared Board is the
       FACES stream's board, not a universal one.
     - INDICATOR: a small shared vocabulary (queued/active/review/parked;
       done covers terminal columns) rolls every visible list up into ONE
       face, /pulse (libs/workstreams pulse-*): one row per stream, coarse
       counts, stale flags, the HUMAN-REVIEW rollup, click-through to the
       native boards.
   The join is the per-list OPTIONAL `status-map` field (JSON object,
   column -> coarse status). Standard columns map by default
   (workstreams/status-map-default); an open column with no mapping reads
   as active; a list overrides once via workstreams/status-map-set. No
   item schema changes; nothing backfilled.
   RETIRED by this decision: the strict rendering contract above — faces
   render their OWN list natively; only /pulse projects across lists.
   NOTE (reconciled with the pipeline-model OBITUARY above): the per-item
   `pipeline` override was retired in the same 2026-10-05 audit, so
   nothing here resurrects it — /pulse projects from each list's columns
   (status-map), never from a per-item pipeline. The CONVERGENCE goal
   above is replaced by: one VOCABULARY for indicators, native machines
   for work.")
  (implements "libs/workstreams/lib.pp pulse-* defines + workstreams/status-map-set + /pulse route")
  (status implemented))


 (section projects-plan
  (doc "DECISION (roerick 2026-10-06): projects are a GROUPING LEVEL above
    lists — Basecamp-campsite shape, spec before build. A project is a
    FIRST-CLASS DATUM, type project (never todo-project: type names bake
    into row paths and agent context; the coupling to todos lives in the
    POINTER, list.project_id, not in the project's name — the coupling is
    one-directional, todos point at projects, a project never knows what
    kind of children it has). Card question (a) resolved: first-class
    datum + uuid pointer; the bare string-field variant is REJECTED —
    denormalized identity: typos mint phantom projects, no metadata home,
    rename = N list writes.")
  (status planned)
  (doc "DATUM — the exact store envelope (no new machinery; a new type value):
    { type: project,
      path: data.s.<space>.<b64(project)>.<hash>,
      body: { title: wyo.town, slug: town, owner: roerick, order: 2,
              color: #0b57a8, archived: #f, notes: campsite board, later } }
    The todo-list datum gains ONE pointer field: project_id (uuid). Items
    unchanged — project inherits through the list. IDENTITY vs ADDRESS:
    the uuid is the identity (every pointer survives any reorganization),
    the path is the address (movable) — the pair is what lets the model
    graduate from pointer to containment without a migration cliff.")
  (doc "PERMISSIONING — the datum's own path is the visibility boundary.
    data.s = shared; the owner's garden = private; the same VIS chokepoint
    (trees.borg, one rim) governs, so private-vs-shared projects need NO
    new permission machinery. When containment lands (lists re-parented
    under the project path), visibility at the project node covers its
    lists AND their items by inheritance — subtree scoping without an ACL
    system; the notes.borg private/instance/world tiers slot here.")
  (doc "SURFACE — one face, the pulse one-scan pattern: project -> streams
    -> counts (queued/active/review/parked/stale) + assignees. Cost: the
    existing items+lists scan plus ONE indexed find by type (project) to
    build the id->project map — no N+1 face. Containment later swaps that
    find for children(projects-path). Defaults: the Board (0b21ffaa) stays
    cross-project intake; existing streams backfill in one pass (glochid/
    ppchat = one project, obsd/mainframe = infra, wyo.town = town); the
    triage pass owns placement of NEW streams.")
  (doc "NON-GOALS — no project-level pipeline, no project-specific states,
    no nesting: project > list > card is exactly two levels of grouping,
    one of state; ZERO new state names in every variant. Notes/docs
    attaching to projects is DEFERRED (card question (c)) — the project
    node's body is the home when it happens. Who may create projects:
    admin/roerick first (question (d)). The /issues register stays
    cross-project (question (b) recommendation stands).")
  (doc "GRADUATION — phase 1: pointer model (project datum + list.project_id).
    phase 2 (with trees.borg): lists re-parent UNDER the project path via
    the tree move op; project_id survives in bodies; the face swaps one
    resolution function and nothing else changes.")
  (doc "DEPENDENCIES + ACCEPTANCE — eb24a8f0 (tree reads) and 42f13855
    (one-scan faces) land or are designed-in first: the project face
    multiplies whatever the stream scan costs. Acceptance: one face where
    roerick sees per-project stream groups with live counts and can jump
    into any stream board; adding a stream to a project is one field
    write; zero new state names."))

)
